hydrapy/cellular.py:
  Adapted from packages/cellular/src/1d.ts and its API/kernel definitions.
  Copyright 2022-2026 Karsten Schmidt.
  Changes: Python/NumPy implementation, bounded row history, fixed-time
  advancement and replay, deterministic initialization/perturbation, glyph
  rendering, and a hydrapy frame-source adapter. Only the public cellular
  engine and its README's two example rules are used. No C-SCAPE or
  ASCII-SCAPE artwork source, curated rule catalog, palette or typeface is
  included.

hydrapy/ops_fields.py, orbitVoronoi source:
  Ring arrangement and alternating rotation adapted from
  examples/rotating-voronoi/src/index.ts (SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0).
  Copyright 2019-2025 Alberto Massa (as stated in the example README).
  The upstream example credits Mike Bostock's rotating-voronoi sketch:
    https://observablehq.com/@mbostock/rotating-voronoi
  and the original ornament by Mario Klingemann:
    https://www.flickr.com/photos/quasimondo/8254540763/
  Changes: analytic NumPy/GLSL nearest-site rasterizer, time-based movement,
  fixed configurable ring counts, cell/edge/distance modes. No upstream
  Delaunay mesh, polygon inset or cubic subdivision implementation is copied.
  This is not the De/Frag renderer.

The new SDF operations, curve helpers and flora adapter are hydrapy code
under the repository's AGPL-3.0-or-later license. They do not bundle source
from FXhash editions. The flora adapter reads the user-owned Generative_Art
wisconsin-flora-1 interchange schema.
